      "signature": "void FUN_100032b0(int * pBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Creates a Windows palette (HPALETTE) from color data in a buffer structure.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Initialize LOGPALETTE structure with version 0x300 (Windows 3.0)\n    2. Read palette entry count from buffer offset 0x2c\n    3. Loop through each palette entry (0x2c total), copying RGB data from buffer:\n       - Source: buffer base + 0x3e (color data starts here)\n       - Each entry is 4 bytes: R, G, B, + 1 reserved\n    4. Set palette flags based on range checks:\n       - If index is within range [0x34, 0x38) of buffer: flag = 0x04 (animated)\n       - Otherwise: flag = 0x00 (normal)\n    5. Call CreatePalette() with initialized LOGPALETTE\n    6. Store returned HPALETTE at buffer offset 0x458\n    7. If buffer type (offset 0x8) is 5 (DIB):\n       - If SetDIBColorTable function pointer exists: call it\n       - Else: call WinGSetDIBColorTable with palette data\n\n  Parameters:\n    pBuffer   Pointer to buffer structure containing color palette data\n              offset 0x8: buffer type (5 = DIB surface)\n              offset 0x2c: number of palette entries\n              offset 0x34: start of animated range\n              offset 0x38: end of animated range\n              offset 0x3c-0x3e: palette entry RGB data (begins at 0x3e)\n              offset 0x45c: destination for DIB color table handle\n              offset 0x458: destination for created HPALETTE\n\n  Returns:\n    void (HPALETTE stored in pBuffer[0x458])\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - If palette entry count is 0 or negative, no entries are copied\n    - Animated palette entries (within range) marked with 0x04 flag\n    - DIB type buffers (type == 5) may trigger alternative color table function",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:e1f4ae37957ffba3287fd7826a9f3f53",
