      "comment": "Allocate memory and track allocation statistics for a Smack handle.\n\nThis function wraps radmalloc to provide internal memory tracking for\nSmack video decoder handles, maintaining both current and peak allocation\nstatistics at offsets 0x480 and 0x4c0 in the Smack structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load current allocation total from pSmack+0x480 (dwCurrentAlloc)\n  2. Add requested dwSize to get new total\n  3. Store new total back to pSmack->dwCurrentAlloc\n  4. Compare new total against peak at pSmack+0x4c0 (dwPeakAlloc)\n  5. If new total exceeds peak, update dwPeakAlloc\n  6. Call radmalloc(dwSize) to perform actual allocation\n  7. Return allocated pointer (or NULL on failure)\n\nParameters:\n  pSmack - Pointer to Smack handle structure containing allocation stats\n  dwSize - Number of bytes to allocate\n\nReturns:\n  void* - Pointer to allocated memory, or NULL if radmalloc fails\n\nSmack Structure Fields:\n  Offset | Field          | Type | Description\n  0x480  | dwCurrentAlloc | uint | Running total of bytes allocated\n  0x4c0  | dwPeakAlloc    | uint | High water mark of allocations",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:a9a858c71208a7ec98494372be7b0971",
