      "name": "DecompressSmackFrame",
      "signature": "void DecompressSmackFrame(Smack * pSmack)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Decompresses a Smack video frame using RLE palette-based decompression.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Reset frame state at Smack+0x41c to zero\n    2. Compute frame index: current_frame (0x374) - start_frame (0xc)\n    3. If frame index < 0, skip (frame not ready)\n    4. Check keyframe flag (0x14 bit 0): if set and first frame, call ReadSmackFrame\n    5. Otherwise call FUN_10005440 for normal frame processing\n    6. Load frame data pointer from Smack+0x3d4\n    7. Read block flags byte at (Smack+0x3e0)[frame_idx]: bits 0-7 indicate 8 data blocks\n    8. For each flag bit, set corresponding block pointer at 0x3e4-0x404\n    9. If bit 0 set (RLE flag): copy 0xc0 (192) dwords from palette to stack\n   10. RLE loop: decompress 0x100 (256) pixels from opcode stream\n       - Opcode bit 7 set: repeat N pixels from current position\n       - Opcode bit 6 set: copy N pixels from backref offset\n       - Otherwise: 3 literal palette indices\n   11. Verify expected frame index (0x3d8) matches actual; set error if mismatch\n\n  Parameters:\n    pSmack (ECX via stack)  Pointer to Smack structure (1220 bytes)\n\n  Returns:\n    void - modifies Smack structure in-place:\n      - Success: Smack+0x68 = 0, block pointers populated\n      - Error: Smack+0x68 = 1, Smack+0x3c4 = 1\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - Frame not ready (negative index): returns immediately\n    - Keyframe detection: routes to ReadSmackFrame for special handling\n    - RLE decompression uses 768-byte stack buffer (192 dwords)\n\n  Structure Layout (Smack offsets accessed):\n    Offset | Size | Description\n    0x0c   | 4    | Start frame index\n    0x14   | 4    | Flags (bit 0 = keyframe processing)\n    0x68   | 4    | Error state (0 = OK, 1 = error)\n    0x6c   | 768  | Palette data (192 RGB triplets)\n    0x374  | 4    | Current frame index\n    0x37c  | 4    | Frame data size\n    0x3c4  | 4    | Secondary error flag\n    0x3d4  | 4    | Frame data pointer\n    0x3d8  | 4    | Expected frame index\n    0x3e0  | ptr  | Block flags array pointer\n    0x3e4  | 32   | Block pointers array (8 pointers)\n    0x404  | 4    | End of frame data pointer\n    0x41c  | 4    | Decompression state\n\n  Global Data:\n    g_aSmackPalette (0x100142e0)  256-byte palette index lookup table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
