      "name": "ReadBufferedSmackFrame",
      "signature": "uint ReadBufferedSmackFrame(SmackBuffer * pSmackBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Reads and buffers the next Smack video frame from file with page-aligned I/O.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. On first frame (offset 0x374 == 0), zero-initialize 0xC1 (193) DWORDs at offset 0x6C\n  2. If frame slot at current index (offset 0x444) is valid (!= -1) and has data at +0x2C:\n     a. Count non-empty frame slots from current index to slot 6\n     b. If count matches g_dwProgressCallbackCount, reset all 7 frame streams via callback\n  3. Sum all queued frame sizes from offset 0x3DC array up to frame count (offset 0x374)\n  4. Check early exit flag (bit 0x200 at offset 0x390); if set, store offset and return 0\n  5. Calculate target file offset: accumulated_sizes + base_offset (offset 0x3CC)\n  6. Buffer management:\n     a. If target within current buffer (0x468 <= target < 0x468+0x460): adjust pointers\n     b. If outside buffer: call SetFilePointer, then ReadFileWithBuffer for unaligned reads\n  7. Handle circular buffer wrap when current pointer exceeds end (offset 0x454)\n  8. Call ReadSmackFrame to process the frame data\n\nParameters:\n  pSmackBuffer (Stack[0x4]) -- Pointer to Smack structure containing file handle, frame queue,\n    and buffer management state\n\nReturns:\n  0: Early exit when bit 0x200 is set in flags\n  uint: Result from ReadSmackFrame indicating frame processing status\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Page alignment: Uses 0x1000 (4KB) pages, handles unaligned offsets with (offset & 0xFFF)\n  - Circular buffer: Wraps pointer when it exceeds buffer end at offset 0x454\n  - Frame callback: Resets streams via g_pfnResetSmackStream when frame count matches threshold\n\nStructure Layout (SmackBuffer/Smack offsets used):\n  Offset  Size  Field               Description\n  0x006C  0x304 aFrameWorkBuffer    Working buffer area (0xC1 DWORDs initialized to 0)\n  0x0374  4     dwFrameIndex        Current frame index/count\n  0x0390  4     dwFlags             Status flags (bit 0x200 = skip processing)\n  0x03B0  4     hFile               File handle for SetFilePointer\n  0x03CC  4     dwBaseFileOffset    Base file offset for frame data\n  0x03D0  4     dwCumulativeOffset  Accumulated offset for frame positioning  \n  0x03D4  4     dwUpdatedOffset     Updated offset after early exit\n  0x03DC  4     pFrameSizes         Pointer to array of frame sizes\n  0x0428  28    aFrameSlots[7]      Array of 7 frame slot pointers\n  0x0444  4     nCurrentSlotIndex   Current frame slot index (0-6 or -1)\n  0x0450  4     pBufferStart        Start of file I/O buffer\n  0x0454  4     pBufferEnd          End boundary for circular wrap\n  0x0458  4     pBufferCurrent      Current read position in buffer\n  0x045C  4     pBufferLimit        Upper limit pointer\n  0x0460  4     dwBufferRemaining   Bytes remaining in buffer\n  0x0464  4     dwBufferSize        Total buffer capacity\n  0x0468  4     dwCurrentFileOffset Current file position",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
