      "name": "InitializeSmackAudioBuffer",
      "signature": "uint InitializeSmackAudioBuffer(Smack * pSmack, byte byAudioTrack)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Initializes the audio playback buffer for a specified Smack audio track.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Ensure Windows sound system is initialized via SmackSoundUseWin if callback not set\n  2. Extract track information from pSmack->abHeader[0x48 + track*4]\n  3. Check if track is enabled (bit 0x40000000) and extract sample rate (bits 0-23)\n  4. Return early if sample rate is 0\n  5. Extract audio format flags from byte at bits 24-31:\n     - Bit 5: Stereo flag (1 = stereo, 0 = mono)\n     - Bit 4: 16-bit flag (1 = 16-bit, 0 = 8-bit)\n  6. Calculate frame size = (stereo+1) * (16bit+1) * sample_rate\n  7. Allocate global audio buffer (0x2000 bytes) if not already allocated\n  8. Get audio context pointer from pSmack->abPadding[-0x5c + track*4]\n  9. Zero-initialize audio context structure (0x25 dwords = 0x94 bytes)\n  10. Calculate buffer sizes:\n      - Offset 0x1c: (framesize * 0x400 * microsPerFrame) / 100000\n      - Offset 0x28: framesize * 0x200\n      - Offset 0x18: ((size_0x1c >> 9) + framesize + 0xfff) & 0xfffff000, minimum 0x2000\n  11. Allocate audio buffer of calculated size\n  12. Set up buffer pointers:\n      - Offset 0x08: buffer start\n      - Offset 0x0c: buffer start (duplicate)\n      - Offset 0x00: size from offset 0x0c\n      - Offset 0x04: end = start + size\n  13. Store audio format parameters:\n      - Offset 0x14 (5): frame size\n      - Offset 0x48: sample rate\n      - Offset 0x50: stereo flag\n      - Offset 0x54: 16-bit flag\n  14. Call sound callback with audio context and microseconds per frame\n  15. If callback fails, free allocated buffer and return error\n  16. Store compressed audio data offset at context+0x38\n  17. Mark this track as first audio track if none set (pSmack->abHeader[0x444] == -1)\n  18. Increment global progress counter and return success\n\nParameters:\n  pSmack         Smack* - Pointer to Smack video context structure (ECX/Stack[0x4])\n  byAudioTrack   byte - Audio track index, 0-6 (Stack[0x8])\n\nReturns:\n  Success: 0x00000001 with incremented counter in upper bytes\n  Failure: 0 if global buffer allocation fails\n           0 if track buffer allocation fails\n           Error code if sound callback fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early with masked track info if sample rate is 0\n  - Initializes Windows sound system on first call\n  - Reuses global audio buffer across all tracks (0x2000 bytes)\n  - Minimum track buffer size enforced at 0x2000 bytes\n  - First enabled audio track is recorded in pSmack->abHeader[0x444]\n\nSmack Audio Context Structure (pSmack->abPadding[-0x5c + track*4]):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Type    Description\n  0x00    4     dwBufferSize    DWORD   Size of audio buffer\n  0x04    4     dwBufferEnd     DWORD   End pointer (start + size)\n  0x08    4     pBufferStart    void*   Audio buffer start pointer\n  0x0c    4     pBufferCopy     void*   Copy of buffer start pointer\n  0x14    4     nFrameSize      int     Audio frame size in bytes\n  0x18    4     dwAllocSize     DWORD   Allocated buffer size (page-aligned)\n  0x1c    4     dwCalcSize1     DWORD   Calculated size parameter 1\n  0x28    4     dwCalcSize2     DWORD   Calculated size parameter 2\n  0x38    4     dwDataOffset    DWORD   Offset to compressed audio data\n  0x48    4     dwSampleRate    DWORD   Sample rate (Hz)\n  0x50    4     dwStereo        DWORD   Stereo flag (0=mono, 1=stereo)\n  0x54    4     dw16Bit         DWORD   Bit depth flag (0=8bit, 1=16bit)\n",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
