      "name": "CheckSoundBufferReady",
      "signature": "uint CheckSoundBufferReady(Smack * pSmack)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Checks if the current Smack sound buffer is ready for processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load sound index from Smack+0x444 (dwCurrentSound)\n  2. Verify index is valid (not 0xFFFFFFFF) and processing flag at +0x44c is clear\n  3. If override flag at +0x448 is clear, return success immediately\n  4. Lookup sound buffer from table at Smack+0x428[index]\n  5. Check buffer processing state at buffer+0x4c\n  6. Call g_pfnGetSoundSize() to get current playback position\n  7. Calculate total position: (buffer+0x28 >> 0xa (10)) + buffer+0x24\n  8. Compare against size; if within bounds, clear override flag and return success\n\nParameters:\n  pSmack  Pointer to Smack structure (via stack at +0x4)\n\nReturns:\n  uint combined value:\n    - Low byte (AL): 1 = success/ready, 0 = failure/busy\n    - Upper 24 bits: Current sound byte offset (from index or GetSoundSize)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Invalid index (0xFFFFFFFF): Returns 0 (failure)\n  - Processing flag set at +0x44c: Returns 0 (failure)\n  - Buffer busy (buffer+0x4c != 0): Returns byte offset with AL=0\n  - Override flag clear: Fast path returns success immediately\n\nStructure Layout (Smack):\n  Offset | Size | Field             | Type   | Description\n  0x428  | var  | aSoundBuffers     | DWORD* | Array of sound buffer pointers\n  0x444  | 4    | dwCurrentSound    | DWORD  | Current sound index (-1 = none)\n  0x448  | 4    | dwOverrideFlag    | DWORD  | Priority/processing override\n  0x44c  | 4    | dwProcessingFlag  | DWORD  | Active processing indicator\n\nStructure Layout (SoundBuffer):\n  Offset | Size | Field             | Type   | Description\n  0x24   | 4    | dwPositionOffset  | DWORD  | Base position offset\n  0x28   | 4    | dwDurationBits    | DWORD  | Duration (bits 10-31) + offset (bits 0-9)\n  0x4c   | 4    | dwBusyState       | DWORD  | Non-zero if buffer is being processed",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:24c4db1b96eb3cd82efed3190f5da50b",
