      "signature": "int FUN_10007300(dword dwUnused1, dword dwUnused2, int nContext, int nMode, dword * pOutput)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Processes rectangle region from Smacker video frame into output buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. State machine check at nContext[0x408]:\n     - State 3: Frame complete, reset to 0 and return\n     - State 1: Invoke callback FUN_10012740, transition to state 2 on success\n     - State 2: Continue processing based on nMode parameter\n  2. Scanline processing (nMode=1):\n     - Iterate callback with row stride\n     - Track minimum/maximum X and Y bounds\n     - Update state to 3 when callback fails\n  3. Block processing (nMode!=1):\n     - Calculate block stride as (height * width * 5) / 4\n     - Process in tiles, update bounds incrementally\n     - Continue until callback returns 0\n  4. Alignment and scaling:\n     - If flag 0x300000 set: multiply final coords by 2\n     - Align start X down to 0x8 boundary if width permits\n     - Align output width up to 0x8 boundary\n  5. Write results to pOutput array (4 DWORDs)\n\nParameters:\n  dwUnused1 (ECX): Unused, always 0\n  dwUnused2 (EDX): Unused, always 0\n  nContext: Base address of context structure\n  nMode: 1=linear scanline mode, else=block tile mode\n  pOutput: Pointer to array for [xMin, yMin, xMax, yMax] coordinates\n\nReturns:\n  Success: EAX=1, output buffer populated with rect coordinates\n  Failure: EAX=0, output buffer zeroed (if nContext[0x68]==0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nContext[0x408]=3 initially, short-circuit returns immediately\n  - Callback failure during state 1 checks nContext[0x68]\n  - Coordinate scaling applied if feature flag 0x300000 enabled\n  - Boundary alignment may reduce rectangle width/height\n\nStructure: nContext offsets:\n  +0x004: Frame height (pixels)\n  +0x068: Control flag (0=early exit path available)\n  +0x390: Feature flags (bit 0x300000=2x scaling)\n  +0x394: Pitch/stride (bytes per scanline)\n  +0x398: Base Y offset\n  +0x408: State (1=initialize, 2=processing, 3=done)\n  +0x40C: Current X coordinate\n  +0x410: Current Y coordinate\n  +0x414: X stride (width increment)\n  +0x418: Y stride (height increment)\n  +0x3BC: Callback context/handle",
