      "name": "MemoryCopyRegions",
      "signature": "void * MemoryCopyRegions(void * pDest, void * pSrcEnd, void * pSrc, int iDestEnd, dword cbSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Copies data between two memory regions with overlapping support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Calculate size available in destination: iDestEnd - pSrcEnd\n  2. If available size >= 0 and source has data (cbSize != 0):\n     a. Copy from pSrcEnd (source pointer) in 4-byte dwords\n     b. Copy remaining 0-3 bytes individually\n     c. Reduce remaining size by copied amount\n  3. If remaining size > 0 (pSrc region):\n     a. Copy pSrc to destination in 4-byte dwords\n     b. Copy remaining 0-3 bytes individually\n     c. Advance destination pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pDest - Destination buffer pointer\n  pSrcEnd - End/pointer within source region (first copy source)\n  pSrc - Start pointer of source region (second copy source)\n  iDestEnd - End of destination buffer\n  cbSize - Number of bytes to copy from pSrc region\n\nReturns:\n  Pointer to end of copied data in destination\n  EAX contains result pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:6a0cf19bda6cf60454178f36cdfa8b4f",
