      "name": "ConfigureSmackAudioSample",
      "signature": "void ConfigureSmackAudioSample(Smack * pSmack)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Configures a Miles Sound System (MSS) audio sample for Smack video playback.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Initialize the AIL sample handle from Smack structure offset 0x40\n    2. Compute sample type based on stereo (offset 0x50) and 16-bit (offset 0x54) flags:\n       - Stereo + 8-bit:  type = 3\n       - Stereo + 16-bit: type = 1\n       - Mono + 8-bit:    type = 2\n       - Mono + 16-bit:   type = 0\n    3. Set sample type and stereo flag via AIL_set_sample_type\n    4. Set playback rate from offset 0x48\n    5. Associate Smack pointer with sample via AIL_set_sample_user_data\n    6. Set initial volume to 0x7f (127, ~50% max)\n\n  Parameters:\n    pSmack - Pointer to Smack structure containing audio configuration\n\n  Returns:\n    void\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - Requires MSS/AIL function pointers to be initialized via SmackSoundUseMSS\n    - Sample handle at offset 0x40 must be valid (allocated via AIL_allocate_sample_handle)\n    - Volume 0x7f (127) is default; max is 0xff (255)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:965397b42f1f9af8f72d3fe7e1959f2a",
