      "name": "InitializeLinkedListNode",
      "signature": "dword InitializeLinkedListNode(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Initializes a linked list node with allocated memory buffers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call initialization callback (g_pfnInitializeCallback) with local data\n2. If callback fails or returns 0xcb, return error code\n3. Calculate scaled value: (wInputValue * field_0x14) / g_dwDivisor\n4. Allocate 0x30 bytes (48 bytes) for primary buffer\n5. Clear allocated buffer using REP STOSD\n6. Allocate additional memory based on scaled value + 0x38\n7. Verify secondary allocation succeeded, return error if NULL\n8. Store configuration data and set magic value 0x81000000\n9. Calculate final scaled value: (g_dwMultiplier * 0x100) / field_0x48\n10. Insert node into linked list via g_pLinkedListHead\n11. Return success status with upper bytes of scaled value\n\nParameters:\n  ESI  pNode - Pointer to structure (accessed with offsets 0x14, 0x44, 0x60, 0x68, 0x3c, 0x48)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX = 0x01 on success with scaled value in upper bytes\n  EAX = error code (bottom 24 bits only) on allocation failure or callback error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Callback may return 0x00 or 0xcb as valid results\n  - Allocation failures at offset 0x60 or offset 0x4 return error\n  - Linked list insertion uses global pointer chain",
