      "name": "ApplyColorScale",
      "signature": "void ApplyColorScale(void * pCallback, uint dwColor, uint dwScale)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Scales color value using 16-bit fixed-point blending arithmetic.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Clamp input color value to 0xFFFF maximum\n  2. If dwScale < 0x8000: apply downscaling (color * scale / 0x8000)\n  3. If dwScale > 0x8000: apply upscaling using complement (0x10000 - scale)\n  4. Right-shift both color components by 8 bits to extract 16-bit values\n  5. Invoke g_pfnColorBlend callback with scaled component parameters\n  6. Return (stdcall cleanup)\n\nParameters:\n  pCallback (EDX): Function pointer to color blending callback routine\n  dwColor (stack): RGB color value, range 0x0000-0xFFFF\n  dwScale (stack): 16-bit fixed-point scale (0x8000=neutral, 0x0000=black, 0x10000=white)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result passed through pCallback invocation with two uint color components",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:0d4062813b83191b8f08e5b01dd66114",
