      "name": "SmackSoundInitialize",
      "signature": "int SmackSoundInitialize(SmackBuffer * pBuffer, dword dwParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes a Smack sound buffer for playback\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Calculate required buffer size from input data size (shift >> 2, round to 0x1000)\n  2. Allocate memory for sound buffer (calculated_size*2 + 0x40 bytes via radmalloc)\n  3. Store allocation pointer in structure at offset +0x64\n  4. Calculate and store buffer end pointer at offset +0x68\n  5. Store custom parameter (dwParam) at offset +0x78\n  6. Call FUN_10008800 to perform internal sound buffer initialization\n  7. If init succeeds, link structure to global linked list via g_pSmackSoundListHead\n  8. If init fails, free allocated memory and return error code\n\nParameters:\n  pBuffer   Pointer to SmackBuffer structure (passed in ESI, contains sound data info)\n  dwParam   Custom parameter value stored at buffer offset +0x78 (purpose varies by caller)\n\nReturns:\n  1 (0x00000001)  - Success: Buffer initialized and linked to list\n  0 (0x00000000)  - Failure: Either radmalloc failed or FUN_10008800 initialization failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If radmalloc returns NULL, function exits immediately with return 0\n  - If FUN_10008800 returns 0 (failure), previously allocated memory is freed before returning 0\n  - Successful init links structure to global list at g_pSmackSoundListHead\n\nStructure Offsets Accessed:\n  Offset | Size | Field             | Type     | Description\n  0x14   | 4    | dwInputDataSize   | DWORD    | Input data size used to calculate buffer\n  0x44   | 4    | dwCalculatedSize  | DWORD    | Calculated buffer size (rounded to 4KB)\n  0x64   | 4    | pAllocatedMem     | void*    | Pointer to radmalloc'ed memory\n  0x68   | 4    | pBufferEnd        | void*    | Buffer end pointer (alloc + size*2 + 0x20)\n  0x78   | 4    | dwCustomParam     | DWORD    | Custom parameter (dwParam)\n  0x3c   | 4    | pNextInList       | void*    | Next buffer in linked list\n",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
