      "name": "CloseWaveOutDeviceCallback",
      "signature": "void CloseWaveOutDeviceCallback(int nAudioContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Stdcall callback wrapper that closes the wave output device.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load nAudioContext parameter from stack [ESP+4]\n  2. Push nAudioContext as argument\n  3. Call CloseWaveOutDevice (cdecl)\n  4. Clean up stack (ADD ESP, 4)\n  5. Return and pop 4 bytes (stdcall convention)\n\nParameters:\n  nAudioContext (int): Base address of audio context structure\n                       Passed via [ESP+4], forwarded to CloseWaveOutDevice\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nNotes:\n  This function is a stdcall-to-cdecl thunk stored in DAT_100142ac.\n  Used as a callback in the Smack sound system.\n  \n  WARNING: Function boundaries appear incorrect in Ghidra.\n  Actual function is 16 bytes (0x10008c80 - 0x10008c8f):\n    10008c80: MOV EAX, [ESP+4]\n    10008c84: PUSH EAX\n    10008c85: CALL CloseWaveOutDevice\n    10008c8a: ADD ESP, 4\n    10008c8d: RET 4",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:546c17e22a38a8e15c8829671ea3e893",
