      "name": "UpdateAudioStreamBuffers",
      "signature": "void UpdateAudioStreamBuffers(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes audio stream buffers at timer intervals, managing fill levels and synchronization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Increment/lock global reference counter\n  2. If first reference, initialize timing: record current time, set base timestamp\n  3. Process linked list of active audio streams if timer interval (10ms) elapsed\n  4. For each stream:\n    a. Call stream update callback (vtable[0x10]) with current time\n    b. Check fill state: if time >= threshold, trigger fill completion\n    c. Check if buffer refill needed (25% threshold) and < 4 pending fills\n    d. If refill: allocate memory, copy data via MemoryCopyRegions to dst\n    e. Mark stream, call completion callback (vtable[0x4c])\n  5. Decrement reference counter, release lock\n\nParameters:\n  (void) - No parameters; operates on global audio stream linked list\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Thread-synchronized via LOCK/UNLOCK (reference counting)\n  - Handles wrap-around for circular buffers (offset 0x74, 0x78)\n  - Supports dual-buffer streaming (primary + secondary regions)\n  - Fill pattern depends on stream flags (offset 0x50)\n  - Prevents recursive entry via counter check\n\nStructure Fields (Stream object at offset from pStream):\n  Offset | Field | Purpose\n  -------|-------|----------\n  0x04   | uSize | Buffer size in bytes\n  0x10   | dwFlags | Control flags\n  0x18   | pVtable | Pointer to callback vtable\n  0x44   | dwMaxFill | Maximum fill size\n  0x50   | dwFillFlag | Fill type indicator\n  0x58   | wActive | Activity flag\n  0x60   | dwLength | Data length\n  0x6c   | dwState | Processing state\n  0x7c   | dwTime | Last process timestamp",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:4c97d39d817c92a9d972856489cf0cc8",
