      "name": "ProcessAudioStreamBuffer",
      "signature": "void ProcessAudioStreamBuffer(int * pAudioStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes an audio stream buffer for playback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Extract audio parameters from input structure (frame count, size, flags)\n  2. Adjust frame byte count: param+0x54 value + 1\n  3. Load frame count from param+0x48\n  4. Calculate frame size: 0x10 if (param+0x50==0), else 0x18\n  5. Compute total buffer bytes: frame_bytes * frame_size * frame_count\n  6. Initialize request descriptor (size=0x14, flags=0x1)\n  7. Atomic increment lock counter for thread safety\n  8. Call pre-lock callback if registered\n  9. Request buffer via audio manager vtable[0xc](manager, descriptor, local_28)\n  10. If allocation fails, call error handler and cleanup\n  11. Atomic decrement lock counter\n  12. Call post-lock callback if registered\n\nParameters:\n  pAudioStream: Pointer to audio stream structure with fields:\n    +0x48: Frame count (DWORD)\n    +0x50: Frame size selector flag (DWORD, 0=use default)\n    +0x54: Frame byte offset adjustment (BYTE)\n\nReturns:\n  void - All operations handled via global callbacks and audio manager\n  \nSpecial Cases:\n  - Uses atomic operations on global lock counter for synchronization\n  - Buffer allocation may fail, triggering error handler\n  - Optional callbacks (pre/post-lock) are null-checked",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:09dd12d1d6afc7cdcffe830ab31d58f5",
