      "name": "InitializeAudioStream",
      "signature": "uint InitializeAudioStream(void * pAudioStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Initialize an audio stream by allocating buffers and configuring audio manager.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Calculate buffer dimensions from stream parameters (sample rate, channels, bits)\n  2. Increment global audio lock counter (g_dwAudioLockCount) via atomic LOCK instruction\n  3. Call pre-lock callback if registered (g_pfnAudioPreLock)\n  4. Request audio manager to allocate primary buffer at offset 0x60 of stream struct\n  5. Call post-lock callback if registered (g_pfnAudioPostLock)\n  6. On allocation failure, request secondary buffer with additional parameter\n  7. Output error code via debug if enabled (g_bDebugAudio == 0x01)\n  8. Initialize stream state fields (0x84=0, 0x6c=1, 0x7c=0xffffffff, 0x8c=0)\n  9. Increment stream counter (g_dwAudioStreamCount @ 0x100148d0)\n\nParameters:\n  pAudioStream (offset +0x4): Pointer to audio stream structure\n    +0x44: Audio manager or descriptor pointer\n    +0x48: Sample rate (samples per second)\n    +0x50: Flags/mode (affects buffer size calculation)\n    +0x54: Bit depth / sample format indicator\n    +0x60+: Buffer allocation area\n    +0x6c: Playback state field\n    +0x7c: Position/status field\n    +0x84: Error code field\n    +0x8c: Completion flag field\n    +0x90: Audio manager interface pointer\n\nReturns:\n  EAX=1 on success (buffer allocated, stream initialized)\n  EAX=0 on failure (buffer allocation failed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Atomic lock counter prevents concurrent audio initialization\n  - Pre/post-lock callbacks allow synchronization with other subsystems\n  - Secondary buffer requested if primary allocation fails\n  - Debug output only if g_bDebugAudio flag is set to 0x01",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:f31778aff00ddc58b34226237ece09c5",
