      "name": "UnlockAudioDevice",
      "signature": "void UnlockAudioDevice(AudioDeviceContext * pAudioDevice)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Unlocks and releases an audio device resource\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if audio device interface pointer is valid at offset 0x60\n  2. If valid, increment global audio lock counter atomically\n  3. Call pre-unlock callback (g_pfnAudioPreLock) if set\n  4. Invoke audio device release method at vtable offset 0x48\n  5. Invoke audio device unlock method at vtable offset 0x08\n  6. Decrement global audio lock counter atomically\n  7. Call post-unlock callback (g_pfnAudioPostLock) if set\n  8. Zero the device interface pointer at offset 0x60\n  9. Decrement global active device counter (g_dwAudioDeviceCount)\n\nParameters:\n  pAudioDevice: Pointer to audio device context structure\n    Offset 0x60 contains pointer to audio device interface\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value; releases resources on success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  If device interface at offset 0x60 is NULL, function returns immediately\n  without performing unlock sequence",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d280d165bc2c8d11536d4fd5f0bfee1b",
