      "name": "AudioSetPan",
      "signature": "void AudioSetPan(int nAudioHandler, dword nVolume, dword nPan)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets audio output pan and volume for a given audio handler with thread-safe locking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Clamp nVolume to maximum 0x8000 (32768)\n  2. Validate audio handler pointer at offset 0x60\n  3. Acquire audio lock and call pre-lock callback\n  4. Calculate pan value: ((nPan * 0x4e20) / 0x10000) - 0x2710 (-10000 to +10000 range)\n  5. Call handler vtable[0x40] with pan value\n  6. Calculate volume: (((nVolume * 0x186a0) / 0x8000) + 5) / 10 - 0x2710 (-10000 to +10000 range)\n  7. Call handler vtable[0x3c] with volume value\n  8. Release audio lock and call post-lock callback\n  \nParameters:\n  pAudioHandler: Handler structure pointer (offset 0x60 points to vtable)\n  nVolume: Volume level 0x0 to 0x8000 (32768=max)\n  nPan: Pan value 0x0 to 0x10000 (65536=center)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If audio handler pointer is NULL, function returns early (no-op)\n  - Lock counting increments/decrements g_dwAudioLockCount for thread safety\n  - Callbacks (g_pfnAudioPreLock, g_pfnAudioPostLock) are optional and checked for NULL",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
