      "name": "ExpandByteToWord",
      "signature": "void ExpandByteToWord(int nUnused1, int nUnused2, uint * pDestBuffer, int nDestPitch, uint * pSrcBuffer, int nSrcPitch, uint nWidth, int nHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "ExpandByteToWord - Expands 8-bit pixels to 32-bit with SIMD optimization\nConverts packed single-byte pixel data to expanded word-sized values\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check for MMX/SIMD capability using DetectSIMDCapabilities()\n  2. If MMX available: process 16 pixels per iteration using MMX registers\n     - Load 8 bytes from source into MM1\n     - Unpack low bytes: PUNPCKLBW (MM1, MM2) \u2192 MM3\n     - Unpack high bytes: PUNPCKHBW (MM1, MM2) \u2192 MM4\n     - Store unpacked words to dual destination buffers\n  3. If MMX unavailable or remainder pixels (width % 4 != 0):\n     - Process 4 pixels per scalar iteration\n     - Double each byte value (0x00\u21920x0000, 0xFF\u21920xFFFF)\n  4. Handle final 1-3 remainder pixels individually\n  5. Advance source/destination pointers by pitch values\n  6. Repeat for each scanline until nHeight iterations complete\n\nParameters:\n  nUnused1 (ECX) - Reserved, not used\n  nUnused2 (EDX) - Reserved, not used\n  pDestBuffer (Stack+0x4) - Pointer to destination buffer 1 (uint array)\n  nDestPitch (Stack+0x8) - Destination buffer row pitch in bytes (typically width*4)\n  pSrcBuffer (Stack+0xC) - Pointer to source buffer (uint array, packed bytes)\n  nSrcPitch (Stack+0x10) - Source buffer row pitch in bytes\n  nWidth (Stack+0x14) - Image width in pixels\n  nHeight (Stack+0x18) - Image height in pixels (number of scanlines)\n\nReturns:\n  None (void function)\n  Side effects: Modifies destination buffer in-place with expanded pixel data\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Width values 1-3: Uses scalar path for remainder pixels\n  - Width < 4: Falls back to scalar expansion for entire image\n  - Zero width/height: Function still executes but processes no data\n  - Non-SIMD capable CPU: Uses scalar (C-like) implementation\n  - Destination buffer overwrite: No bounds checking; assumes buffer large enough\n\nMemory Model:\n  - Source and destination buffers allocated by caller\n  - Function does not allocate or free memory\n  - Two destination buffers processed (typically for deinterlacing)\n  - Caller responsible for buffer lifetime and cleanup\n  - Pitch values allow for non-contiguous memory layouts\n\nUse case: Video decompression/blitting, typically called from _SmackBlit routine\nfor Smacker video codec playback with byte-to-word pixel expansion.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
