      "name": "BlitPalettized8to16",
      "signature": "void BlitPalettized8to16(ushort * pDest, int nDestPitchAdj, byte * pSrc, int nSrcPitchAdj, uint nWidth, int nHeight, ushort * pPalette)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Blit 8-bit palettized pixels to 16-bit RGB destination\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Calculate DWORD count (nWidth/4) and remainder (nWidth%4)\n  2. For each row (nHeight iterations):\n     a. Process nWidth/4 groups of 4 pixels:\n        - Read 4 source bytes as DWORD\n        - Look up each byte in 16-bit palette (offset 0x0-0x1ff)\n        - Write 2 DWORDs (4 pixels) to destination\n     b. Process remaining nWidth%4 pixels (0-3) one at a time:\n        - Read single source byte\n        - Look up in palette, write single 16-bit pixel\n     c. Advance dest/src by pitch adjustments for next row\n\nParameters:\n  pDest (EDI) - Destination buffer for 16-bit RGB pixels\n  nDestPitchAdj - Bytes to add to dest after each row (pitch - nWidth*2)\n  pSrc (ESI) - Source buffer of 8-bit palette indices\n  nSrcPitchAdj - Bytes to add to source after each row (pitch - nWidth)\n  nWidth (ECX) - Width in pixels per row\n  nHeight (EAX) - Number of rows to blit\n  pPalette (EBP) - 256-entry palette table of 16-bit RGB values\n\nReturns:\n  void - Modifies destination buffer in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Width divisible by 4: Fast path only executes\n  - Width < 4: Remainder loop handles all pixels\n  - Zero width or height: Loop skipped entirely\n  - Pitch adjustments handle non-contiguous buffers",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d904867469720f2236a4c11be54bc19e",
