      "name": "ConvertIndexedPixelsToDualBuffer16",
      "signature": "void ConvertIndexedPixelsToDualBuffer16(ushort * pDestBuffer, int nDestRowStride, dword * pSrcPixels, int nSrcRowStride, dword nPixelWidth, int nRowHeight, ushort * pLookupTable)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts 8-bit indexed pixels to 16-bit color with dual-buffer blit operation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Calculate row stride offset: iVar4 = -(nPixelWidth * 4 + nDestRowStride * -2)\n  2. Check feature flag g_dwSIMDFeatureLevel for optimization path selection\n  3. If flag < 0x2 (scalar path):\n     - Process 4 pixels per iteration from pSrcPixels\n     - Lookup each byte index in pLookupTable[index*2] to get 16-bit color\n     - Duplicate 16-bit value to 32-bit DWORD (color | color << 0x10)\n     - Write to pDestBuffer and pDestBuffer[nDestRowStride] simultaneously\n     - Remaining pixels (nPixelWidth & 0x3) handled in cleanup loop\n  4. If flag >= 0x2 (MMX SIMD path):\n     - Process 8 pixels per iteration using MMX instructions\n     - Expand 8 bytes via pLookupTable, pack with PUNPCKLWD\n     - Write 64-bit results with MOVQ to dual buffers\n     - Execute EMMS at 0x1000a317 to clear MMX state before return\n\nParameters:\n  pDestBuffer (ushort*) - destination frame buffer (16-bit color output)\n  nDestRowStride (int)  - destination pitch/stride in bytes between rows\n  pSrcPixels (dword*)   - source 8-bit indexed color pixels (4 bytes per load)\n  nSrcRowStride (int)   - source pitch adjustment between rows\n  nPixelWidth (dword)   - pixel count per row (0x100+ typical)\n  nRowHeight (int)      - number of rows to process\n  pLookupTable (ushort*) - 256-entry palette [index*2] = 16-bit color\n\nReturns:\n  void - modifies pDestBuffer and pDestBuffer[nDestRowStride] with converted pixels\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Non-aligned widths: cleanup loops handle remainders (& 0x3 or & 0x7)\n  - Dual output: writes to both primary and offset buffers in lockstep\n  - SIMD detection: runtime feature flag determines execution path",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:7e293dcb2f80ddd28cdc14be4f4bb87e",
