      "name": "BlitTransparent_SIMD",
      "signature": "void BlitTransparent_SIMD(byte * pDest, int nDestStride, byte * pSrc, int nSrcStride, dword dwWidth, int nHeight, byte byColorKey)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "BlitTransparent_SIMD - SIMD-optimized transparent pixel blit with color key\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check CPU SIMD capabilities (SSE/MMX support) via g_fMMXSupported\n  2. Determine processing path based on width and CPU capabilities\n  3. For scalar path (width < 8 or no MMX):\n    - Iterate height rows, copying bytes\n    - Skip pixels matching color key (0xXX)\n  4. For SIMD path (width >= 8 and MMX supported):\n    - Process 8 bytes per iteration using MMX instructions\n    - Use PCMPEQB to compare against color key\n    - Use PAND/PANDN/POR to conditionally copy pixels\n    - Move to next row after processing width bytes\n  5. Return after all rows processed\n\nParameters:\n  pDest - Destination buffer pointer\n  nDestStride - Bytes to skip between destination rows\n  pSrc - Source buffer pointer\n  nSrcStride - Bytes to skip between source rows\n  dwWidth - Width in pixels/bytes to process per row\n  nHeight - Number of rows to process\n  byColorKey - Pixel value to skip (transparent color)\n\nReturns:\n  void (modifies destination buffer in-place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty dimensions (dwWidth=0 or nHeight=0): No operation performed\n  - MMX unavailable: Falls back to scalar processing\n  - Color key value 0x00: All zero bytes are treated as transparent\n  - Non-contiguous buffers: Stride parameters handle padding/offsets",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d1847c2f87b188f377b796a2d8f4c3ae",
