      "name": "BlendPixelBuffers",
      "signature": "void BlendPixelBuffers(ushort * pDest, int nSrcOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Blends two pixel buffers using color-masked addition and bit shifting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Iterate over rows (uVar2 = 0, step 0x3)\n  2. For each row, iterate over columns (uVar3 = 0, step 0x3)\n  3. Load 32-bit values from both source offsets\n  4. Apply color mask (0xfefefe) to preserve RGB components\n  5. Sum masked values (blend operation)\n  6. Extract and combine bit-shifted components into 16-bit result\n  7. Write result to destination buffer, advance pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pDest - Pointer to 16-bit output buffer\n  nSrcOffset - Base offset into 32-bit source buffers (0x300 bytes max)\n\nReturns:\n  None (void)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Buffer dimensions: 0x300 bytes (768 bytes = 256x3 pixels per scanline)\n  Mask 0xfefefe: Removes LSBs to reduce color channel interference\n  Bit manipulation: Right-shifts extract channels, left-shifts recombine",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:5a79a142d0c1241f91c044994911a678",
