      "name": "QuantizePaletteToRgb",
      "signature": "void QuantizePaletteToRgb(byte * pOutput, byte * pPalette)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Quantizes a 256-color palette into a reduced output palette with nearest-neighbor color matching.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Build sorted palette index by color values (via qsort variant at 0x1000bc00)\n  2. For each output color (0-255):\n     - For each palette index (0-255):\n       - Calculate Euclidean distance in RGB space\n       - Find best match with minimum distance\n       - Store best match index in output palette\n\nParameters:\n  pOutput [ESP+8]: Pointer to 256-byte output palette (quantized color indices)\n  pPalette [ESP+4]: Pointer to 768-byte input RGB palette (256*3 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Output written to pOutput parameter\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Searches palette by sorted indices for optimization\n  - Breaks search early if current color > search value (palette optimization)\n  - Processes full 256x256 lookup table for all colors",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:44167d43a3af793c64b47c52c3cf3d55",
