      "name": "AllocateMemoryWithRetry",
      "signature": "void * AllocateMemoryWithRetry(SIZE_T cbSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates memory with automatic retry logic\nSimple wrapper that delegates to ProcessWithRetry with memory allocator callback\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load memory allocator callback from g_pfnMemAllocator global (0x10015328)\n  2. Call ProcessWithRetry with size parameter and allocator callback\n  3. Return allocation result to caller\n\nParameters:\n  cbSize - Number of bytes to allocate (passed via stack ESP+0x4)\n\nReturns:\n  void* - Pointer to allocated memory on success\n  NULL - If allocation fails after retry logic\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Caller is responsible for freeing allocated memory\n  - If cbSize is 0, behavior depends on ProcessWithRetry implementation\n  - Failed allocations return NULL, not undefined value\n\nCalled By:\n  - InitializeStdioHandles (2 call sites)\n  - ParseCommandLineIntoTokens (2 call sites)\n  - __setargv, GetEnvironmentStringsAsAnsi, radmalloc, FUN_1000cee0\n  - Total: 10 call sites across stdlib initialization and memory management",
