      "name": "ProcessWithRetry",
      "signature": "int ProcessWithRetry(SIZE_T nCount, int nRetry)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Processes a request with optional retry logic until success or max attempts.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Validate nCount is within range [1, 0x20] (32 items max)\n  2. If nCount is 0, normalize to 1\n  3. Loop: attempt primary processing via FUN_1000b940(nCount)\n  4. If successful (non-zero result), return immediately\n  5. If nRetry is 0, exit with 0 (no retries allowed)\n  6. Call FUN_1000c020(nCount) for recovery/reset\n  7. If recovery fails (returns 0), exit with 0\n  8. Continue loop if recovery succeeded\n  9. Return success code from primary process\n\nParameters:\n  nCount - Count/size to process (1-0x20); clamped to 1 if 0\n  nRetry - Retry flag (0=no retry, non-zero=retry on failure)\n\nReturns:\n  Non-zero: Success code from FUN_1000b940\n  0: Validation failed, no retry allowed, or recovery failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - nCount > 0x20: Returns 0 (bounds check failure)\n  - nCount == 0: Normalized to 1 before processing\n  - nRetry == 0: Single attempt mode, no recovery retry",
