      "name": "FreeHeapMemory",
      "signature": "void FreeHeapMemory(void * pMem)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Frees memory previously allocated from the private heap.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Check if pMem is NULL\n    2. If not NULL, call HeapFree with g_hPrivateHeap handle and dwFlags=0x0\n\n  Parameters:\n    pMem - void pointer to memory block to free (can be NULL)\n\n  Returns:\n    void\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - NULL pointer is safely ignored (no-op)\n    - Counterpart to AllocateHeapMemory at 0x1000b940",
