      "name": "QuickSortPartition",
      "signature": "void QuickSortPartition(void * pBase, dword nCount, dword nWidth, void * pfnCompare)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Quicksort implementation using Hoare partition scheme with insertion sort optimization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Validate input: element count >= 2 and element width > 0, else return\n  2. Calculate initial high pointer as (base + (count-1)*width)\n  3. Partition loop: Calculate partition size = (pHi - pBase)/nWidth + 1\n  4. If size > 8: Call swap() for median-of-3 pivot, then partition with two pointers\n  5. If size <= 8: Call FUN_1000bd60 (insertion sort) for final small ranges\n  6. After partition: Push smaller partition to stack, process larger via tail recursion\n  7. Pop stack and repeat until all partitions processed\n\nParameters:\n  pBase [ESP+4]:      Pointer to array base (element 0) - array start address\n  nCount [ESP+8]:     Number of elements to sort - must be >= 2\n  nWidth [ESP+c]:     Size of each element in bytes - must be > 0\n  pfnCompare [ESP+10]: Function pointer to comparison callback\n\nReturns:\n  void - Array sorted in-place in ascending order per comparison function\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  nCount < 2: Early exit without sorting\n  nWidth == 0: Early exit without sorting\n  Size > 8: Uses Hoare partition with median-of-3 pivot selection\n  Size <= 8: Uses insertion sort (FUN_1000bd60) for efficiency",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
