      "name": "InitializeRuntimeEnvironment",
      "signature": "dword InitializeRuntimeEnvironment(dword hModule, dword dwReason)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "CRT runtime environment initialization and shutdown handler.\n\nManages the C runtime library lifecycle for DLL attach/detach operations.\nUses reference counting to prevent redundant initialization and ensure\nproper cleanup sequencing during process termination.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. If dwReason == 0x1 (DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH / Init):\n     a. Call GetVersion() to retrieve Windows OS version information\n     b. If g_dwIsNTInitialized == 0, perform first-time detection:\n        - Check if major version is 0x3 with high bit set (NT 3.x)\n        - Load kernel32.dll and probe for IsTNT() export (Citrix/TNT)\n     c. Call CreatePrivateHeap() to create module heap (0x1000 initial size)\n     d. Parse g_dwWindowsVersion into major/minor/build components\n     e. Increment g_dwInitRefCount to track initialization depth\n     f. Retrieve command line via GetCommandLineA()\n     g. Get environment strings via GetEnvironmentStringsAsAnsi()\n     h. If either cmdline or environment is NULL, cleanup and return 0\n     i. Initialize stdio handles, MBCS table, argv, environment tokens\n     j. Call __cinit() to run C++ static constructors\n  2. If dwReason == 0x0 (DLL_PROCESS_DETACH / Cleanup):\n     a. If g_dwInitRefCount <= 0, return 0 (underflow protection)\n     b. Decrement g_dwInitRefCount\n     c. If g_dwExitSuspended == 0, call ProcessTerminationHandler(0,0,1)\n     d. Call CleanupHandleTable() to free handle table memory\n     e. Call HeapDestroy() to destroy private heap\n     f. Return 1 on success\n  3. Other dwReason values: Return 1 (no-op)\n\nParameters:\n  hModule   (EBX)  - Module handle (HMODULE), unused in function logic\n  dwReason  (ECX)  - Operation code: 1=init, 0=cleanup, other=no-op\n\nReturns:\n  1 (0x1) - Operation succeeded or no-op\n  0 (0x0) - Initialization failed (cmdline/env NULL) or cleanup underflow\n\nGlobal Variables Accessed:\n  Offset     | Name                   | Access | Description\n  -----------|------------------------|--------|----------------------------------\n  0x10015310 | g_dwInitRefCount       | R/W    | Reference count for init/cleanup\n  0x10015314 | g_szCommandLine        | W      | Pointer to environment block\n  0x10015324 | g_dwIsNTInitialized    | R      | NT detection flag (1=TNT, 2=NT3.x)\n  0x10015358 | g_dwWindowsVersion     | R/W    | Raw GetVersion() result, then build\n  0x10015360 | _g_dwWindowsMajorVer   | W      | Major version (bits 0-7)\n  0x10015364 | _g_dwWindowsMinorVer   | W      | Minor version (bits 8-15)\n  0x1001535c | _g_dwWindowsBuildVer   | W      | Combined version (major*256+minor)\n  0x10015390 | g_dwExitSuspended      | R      | Cleanup suspension flag\n  0x10015fb4 | g_szCmdLineBuffer      | W      | GetCommandLineA() result\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Reference counting prevents multiple initializations on nested DLL loads\n  - NT 3.x detection influences error message banner display path\n  - IsTNT() check identifies Citrix/Terminal Server environments\n  - Cleanup is skipped if g_dwExitSuspended is set (abnormal termination)",
