      "name": "ProcessTerminationHandler",
      "signature": "void ProcessTerminationHandler(UINT dwExitCode, int nRunInitializers, int nSuspend)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Exit process handler with conditional cleanup and termination\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check g_dwExitSuspended flag; if set (0x10015394 == 1), call GetCurrentProcess\n     then immediately TerminateProcess(hProcess, dwExitCode) and return\n  2. Set g_dwExitSuspended = 1 (0x10015390) to prevent re-entrance\n  3. Store bSuspend parameter in g_bExitSuspend (0x1001538c)\n  4. If bRunInitializers == 0, execute cleanup chain at 0x10015fa8:\n     - Loop backward through function pointers starting from 0x10015fa4 - 4\n     - Call each non-null function pointer in reverse order\n     - Continue while pointer >= 0x10015fa8 boundary\n  5. Call __initterm to run C++ initializers for two ranges: 0x10014010-0x10014014\n  6. Call __initterm for second range: 0x10014018-0x1001401c\n  7. If bSuspend == 0, set g_dwExitSuspended = 1 and call ExitProcess(dwExitCode)\n     (NOTE: ExitProcess does not return)\n  8. If bSuspend != 0, return normally\n\nParameters:\n  dwExitCode (UINT): Exit code passed to ExitProcess or TerminateProcess\n  bRunInitializers (int): If 0, execute cleanup function pointer chain; if != 0, skip\n  bSuspend (int): If 0, trigger final ExitProcess call; if != 0, return and don't exit\n\nReturns:\n  Returns normally only if bSuspend != 0; otherwise calls ExitProcess (no return)",
