      "name": "ParseCommandLineIntoTokens",
      "signature": "void ParseCommandLineIntoTokens(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Parses command-line string into individual tokens and builds token array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Count non-'=' characters (tokens) in command-line string (0x3d)\n  2. Allocate memory for token array: (count * 4) + 4 bytes (0x4 per pointer + null terminator)\n  3. Store array pointer in g_apszTokens global\n  4. For each token in command-line:\n     a. Skip if character is '='\n     b. Calculate token length using SCASB string scan (0xffffffff)\n     c. Allocate memory for token string\n     d. Copy token bytes using DWORD-aligned memcpy (0x2 byte copies + remainder)\n  5. Store null terminator at end of array\n\nParameters:\n  (none - accesses globals g_szCommandLine and g_apszTokens)\n\nReturns:\n  void. Sets global g_apszTokens to pointer to allocated token array.\n  Calls __amsg_exit(0x9) if allocation fails.\n\nError Handling:\n  Memory allocation failures exit via __amsg_exit(0x9) (out of memory error)\n  \nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty command-line: creates array with single null terminator, calls FreeHeapMemory\n  - Non-contiguous tokens: each token is separately allocated and copied\n  - Tokens can be any length; string length scan handles null terminators",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
