      "name": "GetEnvironmentStringsAsAnsi",
      "signature": "LPSTR GetEnvironmentStringsAsAnsi(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "LPSTR",
      "comment": "Retrieves the process environment block as an ANSI string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check g_dwEnvStringsType to determine which API to use\n  2. If type is 0 (uninitialized):\n     a. Try GetEnvironmentStringsW() first\n     b. If successful, set type to 1 (Wide)\n     c. If failed, try GetEnvironmentStrings() (ANSI)\n     d. If ANSI successful, set type to 2 (ANSI)\n     e. If both fail, return NULL\n  3. If type is 1 (Wide strings available):\n     a. Get wide environment strings via GetEnvironmentStringsW()\n     b. Calculate string block length by scanning for double-null terminator\n     c. Calculate required buffer size: ((end - start) / 2) + 1 wide chars\n     d. Call WideCharToMultiByte() with NULL buffer to get required size\n     e. Allocate buffer via AllocateMemory()\n     f. Call WideCharToMultiByte() to convert to ANSI\n     g. Free wide strings via FreeEnvironmentStringsW()\n     h. Return ANSI buffer (caller must free)\n  4. If type is 2 (ANSI strings only):\n     a. Get ANSI environment strings via GetEnvironmentStrings()\n     b. Calculate block size by scanning for double-null terminator\n     c. Allocate buffer and copy using DWORD-aligned memcpy\n     d. Free original via FreeEnvironmentStringsA()\n     e. Return copied buffer (caller must free)\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  LPSTR - Pointer to allocated ANSI environment block (caller must free)\n  NULL  - On failure (API call failed or allocation failed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - First call auto-detects Wide vs ANSI API availability\n  - Environment block is double-null terminated (each var null-terminated)\n  - Type 2 path uses optimized DWORD-aligned copy (REP MOVSD/MOVSB)\n  - WideCharToMultiByte uses codepage 0 (CP_ACP, system default ANSI)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
