      "name": "SetNTInitializedFlag",
      "signature": "void SetNTInitializedFlag(DWORD dwNTStatus)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets the Windows NT initialization status flag.\n\n  Called during runtime environment initialization to record the detected\n  Windows NT environment type for later use by error message handlers.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Store dwNTStatus value directly to g_dwIsNTInitialized global\n\n  Parameters:\n    dwNTStatus  - NT detection status code:\n                  0x1 = IsTNT function found in kernel32.dll\n                  0x2 = Windows NT 3.x detected (major version 0x3 + high bit set)\n\n  Returns:\n    void\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - Value 0x1 checked by __FF_MSGBANNER to display runtime error banners\n    - Only set during first initialization (when g_dwIsNTInitialized == 0)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
