      "signature": "void FUN_1000ccf0(int nErrorCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Formats and displays a runtime error message dialog based on error code.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Search error code table at g_aErrorCodeTable (0x100155c0) for matching nErrorCode\n  2. If error code found in table:\n     a. Check error handling mode: if console mode (0x1) or NT initialized:\n        - Get console file handle from g_pHandleTable + 0x10 (0xfffffff4 if invalid)\n        - Write error message to console via WriteFile\n     b. Otherwise (dialog mode):\n        - Get module filename with GetModuleFileNameA into buffer szModulePath\n        - If no filename, use default \"<program name unknown>\"\n        - If path length > 0x3c (60), truncate and append \"...\" suffix\n        - Build error message: \"Runtime Error!\n\nProgram: [module]\n\n[error text]\"\n        - Show message box with title \"Microsoft Visual C++ Runtime Library\"\n  3. Special case: error code 0xfc (252) is ignored (no output)\n\nParameters:\n  nErrorCode (EDX) - Runtime error code to look up in error table\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Error code 0xfc is a no-op (skips all message output)\n  - If module filename unavailable, displays default string\n  - If module path exceeds 60 characters, truncates with ellipsis\n  - Uses either console or dialog mode based on g_dwErrorHandlingMode flag",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
