      "name": "MapLocaleStringWithCodePage",
      "signature": "int MapLocaleStringWithCodePage(LCID nLocaleID, UINT nMapFlags, char * lpszSrc, size_t cbSrc, LPWSTR pwszDest, int nDest, UINT nCodePage)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Maps strings with locale-specific case transformation using ANSI or Unicode APIs.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check g_dwLocaleCapability cache (0=uninit, 1=Unicode, 2=ANSI)\n  2. If uninit, test LCMapStringA with 0x100 (LCMAP_UPPERCASE) on empty string\n  3. If ANSI fails, test LCMapStringW; set capability=1 (Unicode) or return 0\n  4. If ANSI succeeds, set capability=2 (ANSI)\n  5. Validate/count source string with _strncnt if cbSrc > 0\n  6. ANSI path (capability=2): call LCMapStringA directly\n  7. Unicode path (capability=1):\n     a. Convert source ANSI to wide via MultiByteToWideChar (flags=0x9)\n     b. Allocate temp buffer for wide chars (cchWide * 2 bytes)\n     c. Apply LCMapStringW to wide string\n     d. If LCMAP_SORTKEY (0x400) not set: allocate output, convert back via WideCharToMultiByte (flags=0x220)\n     e. If LCMAP_SORTKEY set: copy wide result directly\n  8. Free temp buffers and return result length or 0 on failure\n\nParameters:\n  nLocaleID    (LCID, Stack[0x4])   - Locale identifier for mapping rules\n  nMapFlags    (UINT, Stack[0x8])   - Mapping flags (0x100=UPPERCASE, 0x200=LOWERCASE, 0x400=SORTKEY)\n  lpszSrc      (char*, Stack[0xC])  - Source ANSI string\n  cbSrc        (size_t, Stack[0x10])- Source byte count (0=null-terminated)\n  pwszDest     (LPWSTR, Stack[0x14])- Destination buffer (receives ANSI or wide depending on flags)\n  nDest        (int, Stack[0x18])   - Destination buffer size (0=query required size)\n  nCodePage    (UINT, Stack[0x1C])  - Code page (0=use g_dwDefaultCodePage)\n\nReturns:\n  Success: Length of mapped string (characters or bytes)\n  Failure: 0 (capability detection failed, allocation failed, or mapping failed)\n  Query mode: Required buffer size when nDest=0\n\nGlobal References:\n  g_dwLocaleCapability (DAT_10015650) - Cached locale API capability flag\n  g_dwDefaultCodePage  (DAT_10015348) - Default code page for conversions\n\nCalled By:\n  _tolower @ 0x1000c070\n\nCalls:\n  LCMapStringA, LCMapStringW    - Win32 locale mapping\n  MultiByteToWideChar           - ANSI to Unicode conversion\n  WideCharToMultiByte           - Unicode to ANSI conversion\n  AllocateMemoryWithRetry       - Internal heap allocator\n  FreeHeapMemory                - Internal heap deallocator\n  _strncnt                      - String length with limit",
