      "signature": "LPVOID FUN_1000d4b0(int nElementCount, int nElementSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "LPVOID",
      "comment": "Allocate memory for an array of elements\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Multiply nElementCount \u00d7 nElementSize to get total allocation size\n  2. Ensure minimum allocation of 1 byte (if result is 0)\n  3. Validate size against limit (0xffffffe1 bytes = 4,294,967,265)\n  4. Attempt allocation from private heap with HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY flag\n  5. If successful, return pointer; otherwise invoke error handler\n  6. Retry allocation loop until success or handler returns 0\n\nParameters:\n  nElementCount - Number of elements (int)\n  nElementSize  - Size of each element in bytes (int)\n\nReturns:\n  LPVOID - Pointer to allocated memory on success, NULL on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Size overflow check: rejects allocations > 0xffffffe1\n  - Zero-byte allocation: minimum 1 byte allocated\n  - Allocation failure: invokes g_dwMemAllocator error handler\n  - Handler retry loop: continues until handler returns 0 or allocation succeeds",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
