      "name": "DecompressBitstream",
      "signature": "int DecompressBitstream(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Decompresses variable-length encoded bitstream data using bit extraction and output buffering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize output (EAX = 0x80000000) and push stack markers (-0x1, -0x2)\n  2. Read source dwords from pSourceData when bit buffer is exhausted\n  3. Extract bits from buffer using decremented bit counter (dwBitCount)\n  4. If LSB set: push output pointer to marker stack, advance pOutputData\n  5. If LSB not set: extract byte data with variable bit widths (8-24 bits)\n  6. Write output bytes to pOutputData, update link pointers on marker pops\n  7. Continue until terminator marker (-0x1) reached, return final value\n\nParameters:\n  ESI: Pointer to source compressed data (uint*)\n  EDI: Pointer to output decompressed data (int*)\n  [0x10014ac0]: Global bit count/buffer refill counter (byte)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: Final decompressed value (int)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Bit buffer refill when counter reaches zero (reads next source dword)\n  Variable-width output encoding (8 or 24 bit widths based on buffer state)\n  Link pointer tracking for jump offset encoding (-0x2 marks link positions)\n  Bit shift operations with dynamic counts (CL register for variable shifts)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
