      "name": "BuildHuffmanTree",
      "signature": "int BuildHuffmanTree(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Builds a Huffman tree structure by reading bits from a compressed bitstream.\n\n  Algorithm:\n  1. Initialize return value to 0x80000000 (leaf marker)\n  2. Push sentinel values -1 (end marker) and -2 (leaf placeholder) onto stack\n  3. Loop: decrement global bit counter, refill from ESI if exhausted\n  4. Shift EBP right by 1, check carry (extracted bit)\n  5. If bit=1: pop stack, if -2 push current EDI as leaf position, advance EDI\n  6. If bit=0: pop stack, if -1 exit, else read 8-bit symbol value\n  7. For 8-bit read: if bit counter < 9, refill from next DWORD\n  8. Store symbol at current tree position, update parent offset\n\n  Parameters:\n    ESI - Pointer to compressed input data (DWORD-aligned)\n    EDI - Pointer to output tree node array (int*)\n    EBP - Current bit buffer (32 bits)\n\n  Returns:\n    EAX - Last written tree node value (with 0x80000000 marker for leaves)\n\n  Special Values:\n    0xFFFFFFFE (-2) - Leaf node placeholder on stack\n    0xFFFFFFFF (-1) - End-of-tree sentinel marker\n    0x80000000 - High bit indicates leaf node in output\n\n  Global State:\n    g_byBitCount (0x10014ac0) - Remaining bits in buffer (0x20 when full)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:44f46ef527bad070016e875770123fc1",
