      "name": "ProcessSearchPattern",
      "signature": "void ProcessSearchPattern(dword dwPattern, dword * pBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes search patterns in binary tree structure by iterating through indexed levels.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter from global count (DAT_10014ab4)\n2. Store input buffer pointer to global (DAT_10014a68)\n3. For each iteration (top to bottom):\n   a. Load value from current buffer position\n   b. If lower 0xffff bits are zero (0x0000):\n      - Shift right 0xd (13), mask with 0xffff8\n      - Check bit pattern using decrement counter\n   c. Choose offset 0x4 or shifted value based on lowest bit\n   d. Advance to next tree node\n   e. Repeat until value has non-zero low bits\n4. Store result (pointer offset and depth) to output array\n5. Decrement counter and continue for all indexed levels\n\nParameters:\n  dwPattern = ECX: unused in decompilation, passed via fastcall\n  pBuffer = EDX: pointer to search buffer array\n\nReturns:\n  Results written to EDI (implicit register parameter)\n  Output array: stores offset and depth for each level\n\nMemory Access:\n  Reads: DAT_10014ab4 (count), DAT_10014a68, DAT_10014ab0, DAT_10014a94\n  Writes: results via EDI",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
