      "signature": "void FUN_1000e530(void * this, void * pThis, int * pHuffmanTable1, int * pHuffmanTable2, dword dwBitDepth, dword dwLevelCount, dword dwParam5, dword dwParam6)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize Huffman decompression tables and structures for bit stream decoding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Store input parameters (huffman tables, bit depth, level counts) in global state\n  2. Set up huffman table pointers: pHuffmanTable1 and pHuffmanTable1 + 0x200\n  3. Set default bit count (0x1) and search depth (0xc) in global state\n  4. Call DecompressBitStreamData 4x with varying depths (0xc, 0xc, 0xc, 0xa)\n  5. Copy output array data (0x10 DWORDs) to output buffer + offset 0xd014\n  6. Zero initialize 0x800 (2048) DWORDs in huffman table array\n  7. Call FUN_1000e880 four times to process/validate tables\n  8. Find last non-0xffffffff entry, calculate bit position (shift left 3, bit scan)\n  9. Store bit position at output buffer + 0xd010\n  10. Call FUN_1000e8b0 four times for final processing\n\nParameters:\n  pThis: this pointer (__thiscall convention, ECX register)\n  pHuffmanTable1: huffman table 1 pointer array (0x200 entries)\n  pHuffmanTable2: huffman table 2 pointer array (0x200 entries)\n  dwBitDepth: bit depth for initial tables (0xc = 12 bits)\n  dwLevelCount: huffman level count for first 3 tables (0x1000)\n  dwParam5: parameter for 3rd decompression table\n  dwParam6: parameter for 4th decompression table\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:5a8e6b8851902e07b2b2ccdf4afd6ff0",
