      "name": "InitializeHuffmanTableEntries",
      "signature": "void InitializeHuffmanTableEntries(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes Huffman table entries with bit position values.\n\n  Algorithm:\n  1. Calculate table base at offset 0xD068 from context pointer (ESI)\n  2. Divide byte count (EAX) by 4 to get entry count (SHR 2)\n  3. For each 4-byte entry in the table:\n     a. If entry's low bit (flag) is 0: write current bit position to entry\n     b. If entry's low bit (flag) is 1: copy value from entry offset +2 to offset +0\n  4. Decrement counter and loop until all entries processed\n\n  Parameters:\n    in_EAX    - dwByteCount: Total size in bytes (divided by 4 for entry count)\n    unaff_ESI - pHuffmanContext: Base pointer to Huffman context structure\n\n  Returns:\n    void\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - Uses register-based parameter passing (EAX, ESI)\n    - Preserves EBP across the function (PUSH/POP)\n    - Early exit if counter reaches zero in inner while loop\n    - Flag bit determines whether to initialize or preserve existing value",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
