      "signature": "ulonglong FUN_10011ab0(dword dwUnused1, dword dwUnused2, dword * pBitstream, int pHuffmanBuffer, byte * pFrameInfo)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "ulonglong",
      "comment": "Decodes a single Smacker video frame using Huffman decompression.\n\n  Algorithm:\n  1. Store buffer base pointer and initialize Huffman lookup tables\n  2. Copy 16 entries (4 iterations x 4 entries) from buffer+0xD014 to g_HuffmanTable1Data\n  3. Setup 4 Huffman tree pointers at offsets 0x10, 0x4010, 0x8010, 0xC010\n  4. Parse frame flags from pFrameInfo:\n     - Byte 0, bit 0: Streaming mode (inverted - 0=streaming, 1=non-streaming)\n     - Byte 2, bit 7: Double-Y mode (interlaced scaling)\n     - Byte 1, bit 0: Interlaced mode\n  5. Select appropriate decode handler table based on mode flags\n  6. For non-streaming mode: Extract frame dimensions from pFrameInfo+0x8 through +0x1C\n  7. For streaming mode: Process command stream with special codes:\n     - 0xFFFD: Call stream callback\n     - 0xFFFE: Update frame parameters\n     - 0xFFFF: End of stream\n  8. Detect CPU SIMD capabilities (MMX vs non-MMX)\n  9. Initialize decode entry points based on SIMD level:\n     - Level < 2: Use non-SIMD handlers at 0x1000E8E0, 0x1000E9E0, 0x1000EB90\n     - Level >= 2: Use MMX handlers at 0x1000ED40, 0x1000EE40, 0x1000F010\n  10. Begin Huffman bit-stream decoding via jump table dispatch\n\n  Parameters:\n    dwUnused1 (ECX) - Reserved, not used by function\n    dwUnused2 (EDX) - Reserved, not used by function\n    pBitstream - Pointer to compressed bitstream data\n    pHuffmanBuffer - Base address of Huffman decode buffer (size 0xD054)\n    pFrameInfo - Pointer to frame descriptor structure\n\n  Returns:\n    Low 32 bits: Pointer to output buffer or decode result\n    High 32 bits: Additional state (varies by decode path)\n\n  Frame Info Structure Layout (pFrameInfo):\n    Offset|Size|Field|Type|Description\n    0x00|1|flags0|byte|Bit 0: streaming mode (inverted)\n    0x01|1|flags1|byte|Bit 0: interlaced mode\n    0x02|1|flags2|byte|Bit 7: double-Y scaling mode\n    0x04|4|pfnCallback|ptr|Stream callback function (streaming mode)\n    0x08|4|dwWidth|dword|Frame width in pixels\n    0x0C|4|dwHeight|dword|Frame height in pixels\n    0x10|4|dwStride|dword|Row stride in bytes\n    0x14|4|dwPadLeft|dword|Left padding amount\n    0x18|4|dwBlocks|dword|Number of 4x4 blocks\n    0x1C|4|dwPadRight|dword|Right padding amount\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - Returns early at LAB_10011ed0 for streaming mode end-of-stream\n    - Non-SIMD path uses 32-bit register operations\n    - MMX path uses 64-bit MOVQ for bitstream reads",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
