      "name": "SmackRemapFramePalettes",
      "signature": "void SmackRemapFramePalettes(Smack * pSmack, byte * pbRemapTable)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Remaps color palettes across 4 Smack video frames using a lookup table\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load palette transparency key (0xD010) from Smack structure into g_wBitPosition\n  2. Initialize remap cache from first byte of pbRemapTable at stack offsets\n  3. Process frames 0-3 sequentially:\n     a. Calculate frame offset: base + accumulated size from previous frames\n     b. Convert frame size to dword count (divide by 4)\n     c. Load frame pixels 2 at a time via LODSD (hardware string instruction)\n     d. For each pixel pair:\n        - If low word equals palette key, skip remapping\n        - Lookup transformed color via pbRemapTable[original_color]\n        - Write remapped pixels back to frame buffer in-place\n  4. Frame 4 uses 3-bit indexed format with special 0x3 value check\n  5. Return void\n\nParameters:\n  pSmack (EDI+0x8)        Pointer to Smack video structure\n                          Contains frame offsets at +0x0/+0x4/+0x8/+0xC\n                          Palette key stored at +0xD010\n                          Frame pixel data starts at +0xD068\n  pbRemapTable (EDI+0xC)  256-byte color remapping lookup table\n                          Indexed by original color (0-255)\n                          Returns transformed color value\n\nReturns:\n  void (modifies Smack frame buffers in-place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Palette key in g_wBitPosition marks transparent pixels (not remapped)\n  - Frame 4 only remaps pixels where (pixel & 0x3) == 0x3\n  - Uses LODSD for 2-pixel-at-a-time processing (both low/high bytes)\n  - Frame sizes must be dword-aligned for correct operation\n\nMemory Model:\n  - Modifies Smack frame buffers in-place\n  - Global g_wBitPosition (0x10014ad0) used as palette transparency key\n  - Register-only computation, no stack locals\n  - 6 registers saved/restored (EBP, EDI, ESI, EBX, EDX, ES)\n  - Uses CLD to ensure forward direction for LODSD\n\nSmack Structure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field             Type      Description\n  ------  ----  -----             ----      -----------\n  +0x0    4     dwFrame0Offset    DWORD     Offset to frame 0\n  +0x4    4     dwFrame1Size      DWORD     Frame 1 size in bytes\n  +0x8    4     dwFrame2Size      DWORD     Frame 2 size in bytes\n  +0xC    4     dwFrame3Size      DWORD     Frame 3 size in bytes\n  +0xD010 2     wPaletteKey       WORD      Transparency key (in g_wBitPosition)\n  +0xD068 var   abFrameData       byte[]    Pixel data for all frames\n",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
