      "name": "DetectSIMDCapabilities",
      "signature": "void DetectSIMDCapabilities(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Detects CPU SIMD (SSE) capabilities by testing CPUID and EFLAGS ID bit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if feature flags already initialized (0x2 bit in g_dwCPUFeatureFlags)\n  2. If not, set initialization bit and test EFLAGS ID bit manipulability (0x200000)\n  3. If ID bit is writable, execute CPUID instruction with EAX=1\n  4. Extract SSE support (EDX bit 0x17) and merge into feature flags\n  5. Set global SIMD level: level 1 if flags==2, level 2 if flags==3\n\nParameters:\n  none\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function performs CPU feature detection via CPUID instruction\n  - Tests EFLAGS.ID bit to determine CPUID support\n  - Stores results in globals g_dwCPUFeatureFlags and g_dwSIMDFeatureLevel\n  - Called during initialization by multiple image processing functions",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:2fe2f360db7bd71c43d33230cbd2ddc0",
