      "signature": "int FUN_10012a1f(uint dwMMXMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Configures MMX instruction usage by modifying CPU feature flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. If dwMMXMode == 0: Enable MMX by setting bit 0x4 in g_dwCPUFeatureFlags\n  2. If dwMMXMode == 1: Disable MMX by clearing bit 0x4 (mask 0xfffffffb)\n  3. If dwMMXMode >= 2: Leave flags unchanged\n  4. Call DetectSIMDCapabilities() to recalculate SIMD feature level\n  5. Return 1 if SIMD level is 2 (full capabilities), otherwise 0\n\nParameters:\n  dwMMXMode - MMX configuration mode:\n              0 = Enable MMX (set bit 0x4)\n              1 = Disable MMX (clear bit 0x4)\n              2+ = Query only (no change)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - MMX is available and enabled (SIMD level 2)\n  0 - MMX not available or disabled\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Bit 0x4 in g_dwCPUFeatureFlags controls MMX usage preference\n  - Actual MMX availability depends on CPU detection via CPUID\n  - Called by _SmackUseMMX@4 wrapper function",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:e15678e456b1080a89a68355d5723ec2",
